.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt IMT 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imt
.Nd I2C Windows Precision Touchpad pointer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "imt* at ihidev?"
.Cd "wsmouse* at imt? mux 0"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver reads Windows Precision Touchpad contact reports through
.Xr ihidev 4 .
It sends relative pointer motion and the physical left button to
.Xr wsmouse 4 .
It can generate a left click from a short single-finger tap.
.Pp
The driver requires complete parallel contact reports.
It rejects frames with an invalid size, excessive contact count,
duplicate contact identifiers, or coordinates outside the descriptor ranges.
Hybrid reports, multitouch gestures, and tap dragging are not supported.
.Pp
The driver selects Precision Touchpad input mode when the device opens.
The first contact sets the motion origin.
It does not move the pointer until a subsequent contact report arrives.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
Each device provides
.Va hw.imtN.tapping .
The default value is zero.
Set it to one to enable single-finger tap clicks.
Taps longer than 180 milliseconds do not click.
Motion beyond 50 native coordinate units cancels the tap.
Multiple fingers, a physical button press, or a low-confidence contact also
cancel the tap.
.Pp
Use
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
to preserve the setting across boots.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ihidev 4 ,
.Xr wsmouse 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The driver uses the Windows Precision Touchpad report model from
.Ox
.Nm
and
.Nm hidmt .
This implementation uses the
.Nx
HID parser and wscons pointer interface.
